# config/reciprocal-pending.allow
#
# Operator pages that the reciprocal-aside contract names but that nobody has
# written yet. Format: one slug per line with a trailing "# reason" comment
# (required). Read by bin/check-frontmatter.mjs, assertion 6.
#
# The contract (audit §4.4, plan rule 2) is that a hosted feature page and its
# operator counterpart each carry a note aside pointing at the other. The table
# of pairs lives in bin/check-frontmatter.mjs as RECIPROCAL_PAIRS; this file
# holds only the half of it that does not exist on disk yet.
#
# Why a list and not silence: an aside cannot point at a page that has not been
# written, so the check has to tolerate the gap — but tolerating it silently
# means the assertion never fires at all, including on the day the page finally
# lands. So the gap is declared here instead, and the check fails BOTH ways:
#
#   * a slug in RECIPROCAL_PAIRS that exists neither on disk nor in this file
#     fails, so a new pair cannot be added and left untracked;
#   * a slug listed here whose page now EXISTS fails, so landing the page forces
#     you to delete its line, which in turn turns the reachability assertion on
#     for that pair in the same commit.
#
# Deleting a line is therefore part of writing the page, not a follow-up. The
# reason column says which phase owns it, so the list reads as a work queue.

features/custom-domains # Phase 3 features group, unwritten
features/branding # Phase 3 features group, unwritten
features/incoming-secrets # Phase 3 features group, unwritten
features/interface-and-homepage # Phase 3 features group, unwritten
features/multi-region # Phase 3 features group, unwritten
features/billing-and-entitlements # Phase 3, blocked on the production billing catalog
configure/email # Phase 3 configure group, unwritten
configure/authentication # Phase 3 configure group, unwritten
configure/sso # Phase 3 configure group, unwritten
configure/secret-options # Phase 3 configure group, unwritten
